---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';import {evidence,url} from '../lib/data';const datasets=[...new Set(evidence.observations.map((r:any)=>r.dataset))] as string[];
---
<Layout title="Coverage and limitations"><div class="eyebrow">What is observed—and what is missing</div><h1>The limits are part<br/>of the findings.</h1><p class="lede">The research cutoff is October 19, 2026. Each dataset ends at its own date, often earlier. No full-year 2026 trend is presented.</p><div class="grid"><section class="card"><h3>0 · Zero</h3><p>A source explicitly reports none for a defined measure and period. It is a real observation, not an empty cell.</p></section><section class="card"><h3>— · No data</h3><p>The quantity is not observed, retrieved or validated. It cannot be interpreted as zero or as no effect.</p></section><section class="card"><h3>N/A · Not applicable</h3><p>A measure does not apply to that record, such as a sampling interval for an exact statutory date.</p></section></div>
<section class="section"><h2>Actual data coverage</h2><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Dataset</th><th>Period in this release</th><th>Unit of record</th></tr></thead><tbody>{datasets.map(d=>{const rows=evidence.observations.filter((r:any)=>r.dataset===d);return <tr><td>{d}</td><td>{Math.min(...rows.map((r:any)=>r.year))}–{Math.max(...rows.map((r:any)=>r.year))}<br/>{d.includes('USSC')?'FY2011–FY2014 pooled; 2014 is period end':[...new Set(rows.map((r:any)=>r.periodType))].join(', ')}</td><td>{[...new Set(rows.map((r:any)=>r.unit))].join('; ')}</td></tr>})}</tbody></table></div><p class="small">A single-year snapshot is not a trend. See record notes for periods pooled across several years, source revisions and category changes.</p></section>
<section class="section"><h2>Evidence still needed</h2><div class="grid two">{evidence.gaps.map((g:any)=><article class="card"><h3>{g.topic}</h3><p>{g.detail}</p><p><b>Needed:</b> {g.neededData}</p><p class="small"><b>Implication:</b> {g.impact}</p></article>)}</div></section><section class="section"><h2>What this release cannot conclude</h2><p class="prose">It cannot estimate the national amount of suffering prevented, rank presidents on a common welfare scale, establish a PACT deterrence effect, infer shark mortality from declared fin trade, or assign changes in reported research-animal counts to FDA reform. It cannot infer improved compliance from fewer citations without inspection coverage and selection information. Outcomes after removal from danger remain unknown where placement and follow-up records are absent.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href={url('data/evidence_gaps.csv')} download>Download the gap register</a><a class="button secondary" href={url('methods/')}>Read the methods</a></div></section></Layout>
